From a6e5045fd9a7f08582c76067839c55db95f07f38 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 6a0 <87043474+6a0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 10:14:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 125/128] glm cuda: TF_GLM_SNAP_SUB=1: prompt states kept and
 resumed on TF_GLM_CHUNK rows (EXPERIMENTAL, not built or run)

Kept prompt states sit on the 4,096-row chunk grid (cuda_native.snap_grid), so every turn of a conversation prefills
up to 4,095 trailing tokens again. Measured on this pair's own log (706 single-stream turns of an agent loop,
2026-11-14): TTFT = 0.39-0.52 s + 0.73-0.79 ms a re-prefilled token, a mean tail of ~2,050 tokens beyond the turn's
new ones, i.e. ~1.5 s of every turn's first token and of GPU time the other streams wait through.

0110 (TF_GLM_CHUNK_SOLO) already takes a chunk in busy steps of TF_GLM_CHUNK rows with every state byte equal to the
whole chunk's (glm-solo-check), a busy step commits its rows as a chunk does, and the index rings rebase only at a
chunk's start (prompt_solo.ringsAgree), so the state a pass stands at after a busy step is the one every pass has
there. With TF_GLM_SNAP_SUB=1 (needs TF_GLM_CHUNK_SOLO=4096; TF_GLM_CHUNK=1024 for the finest grid) rank 0:

- plans the cache's marks on TF_GLM_CHUNK rows (cuda_native.snapGrid -> native/cuda_snaps cacheRules), and resumes
  kept states there (cuda_lanes.resumeFrom);
- takes busy steps where a mark lies inside the chunk, so a step starts at the mark and Engine.prefillChunk keeps the
  state there, and to finish a chunk begun in busy steps (prompt_solo.busyAt, as before); a pair never passes a mark;
- no longer takes busy steps merely beside a decoding stream (that behaviour of TF_GLM_CHUNK_SOLO alone was measured
  as no gain here, RESULTS.md 0110), so a chunk without a mark in it goes whole as today;
- runs a whole pass (a warm turn, TF_GLM_PROMPT_STEPS=0) as its steps, since Engine.prefill's chunk loop on every
  rank takes whole chunks only.
Every rank accepts a resume on TF_GLM_CHUNK rows once busy steps are on (Engine.prefillStart, prompt_solo.stepGrid):
the fingerprint already carries the chunk words, so no rank can disagree and its layout is unchanged. Off with image
rows (a busy step takes none) and TF_GLM_KV_SHARD. Unset: every path is as before (subOn false: markWithin false,
snapGrid and the store's grid 4,096; stepGrid is 4,096 unless TF_GLM_CHUNK_SOLO is set).

Cost to weigh: each prompt step has a fixed part (about 0.3 s here), so a tail takes ceil(rows / TF_GLM_CHUNK) steps
where it took one, and states are kept about four times as often (a device copy of the whole state each, and a disk
write with --learn-conversations).

NOT COMPILED OR RUN (no toolchain on the host it was written on). Before use: build, cuda_prompt_solo's unit test,
then on the pair a glm-solo-check style twin (a prompt resumed from a state kept part way into a chunk against the
same prompt cold: first token, next window's logits, ring bases, state bytes), greedy hashes, and the cold/warm
replay with cached counts.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
